Controller AccessControl integration tests
------------------------------------------
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.adminSeesAdminOptions - admin menu shows the admin-only options
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.standardUserSeesNoAdminOptions - standard menu hides the admin-only options
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.addEntryRejectsStandardUser - standard user cannot add, store untouched
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.manageAccessPromotesWithRealRoles - promote makes a standard user an admin
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.manageAccessDemotesWithRealRoles - demote takes admin back to standard
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.manageAccessRejectsNonAdminCaller - only an admin can promote or demote
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.manageAccessRejectsSelfDemotion - an admin cannot demote themself
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.createUserRejectsStandardUser - standard user cannot create users
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.reviewAuditLogRejectsStandardUser - standard user cannot review the audit log
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.browseMainMenuHidesAddEditForStandardUser - add and edit only on the admin browse menu
ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest.listUsernamesExcludesCaller - admin list leaves the caller out
Notes: real AccessControl with in-memory roles (admin boss,
standard alice and bob) behind the full Controller; users,
store, audit, and messages stay mocked.
Run: .\gradlew test --tests "control.ControllerAccessControlIntegrationTest" --console=plain
